  data: {
    LLM: "Don't take the bid unless you have ~60 points in hand (including potential melds). The Jack is crucial (20 pts).\n\nThe 'Schmeiss' Bluff: Offering to throw in the hand (Schmeiss) usually implies a weak hand with trumps, but can be a bluff to get out of a mediocre deal. Opponent must decide to accept the restart or force you to play (often making the suit trump automatically).\n\nEndgames: With 9 cards, counting is exact. You can calculate if the opponent *must* hold the Ten or Ace based on previous tricks. Squeeze them by leading a suit they must trump.",
